---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Hannah Lewis — The Makers Collective | Waiheke Island Art"
  description="Hannah Lewis is a printmaker with The Makers Collective, working from Waiheke Island, New Zealand."
>
  <section class="wrap artist">
    <h1>Hannah Lewis</h1>
    <p>
      Hannah Lewis works in bold, flat colour — screenprints and linocuts
      built from the shapes she sees in Waiheke's vineyards and olive
      groves: rows, terraces, repeated lines running toward a horizon. She
      trained in graphic design before moving into fine art printmaking,
      and that background shows in how deliberately she plans a piece
      before ever touching ink, often working through a dozen small studies
      before committing to a final block.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every print in a run is pulled by hand in Hannah's studio, a small
      edition at a time, and she keeps meticulous records of each one —
      which is why her numbering is exact and her runs never quietly get
      extended. She limits herself to four or five colours per print, a
      constraint she's kept for years because, in her words, "more colours
      just means more decisions, and I'd rather make fewer, better ones."
    </p>
    <p>
      Hannah moved to the island in 2019 after a decade in Wellington, and
      cites the change in landscape — from hills and harbour to rows of
      vines and long flat light — as the reason her work shifted from
      portraiture toward the abstract, pattern-based prints she's known for
      now. She teaches a small printmaking class from her studio most
      Saturdays.
    </p>
    <a href="/gallery" class="btn">View available work</a>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .artist { padding: 4rem 0 5rem; max-width: 58ch; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; }
  .artist h1 { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .artist p { text-align: left; }
  .artist .btn { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
